In an era of rapid technological evolution, few debates have ignited as much confusion as the link between 5G infrastructure and viral infections. Critics argue that the rollout of 5G networks coincided with surges in reported cases, leading some to fear that electromagnetic radiation poses a public health threat. However, the scientific consensus remains grounded in rigorous analysis and peer-reviewed data.

@MediaLab

