To understand the phenomenon, one must examine the transmission patterns of the virus itself. Unlike airborne pathogens, COVID-19 spreads through respiratory droplets and aerosols, which can survive significant periods on surfaces or in the air. The transmission efficiency of viruses decreases significantly with distance and time, meaning the virus cannot travel as far as a radio wave can.

@MediaLab

